|WKO=====================================================================
|YKOSigils are arcane markings worked into rare equipment.
Each marking carries a level. While you wield, wear, or internally bind the
item, its levels count toward your total for that sigil. Marked pieces work
as a set: equip several and their levels add together, up to the sigil's
maximum useful level.

Sigils are part of an item as it is found - you cannot inscribe them
yourself. A sigil briefly glows when you pick up a marked item. Examine a
piece of equipment to see any recognized markings it bears, each listed with
its level and that sigil's maximum.
Ordinary marked equipment usually supplies one level, so building around a
sigil means choosing several compatible pieces. Marked gear can be found in
both older and newer regions. A few powerful signature items supply two
levels from one item.

Some sigils may be occult. Their markings and effects cannot be identified,
and they do not appear in your catalog until your character uncovers the
secret that reveals them. Discovery is permanent for that character.
Unrecognized markings still function and still count toward equipment power.

|WKBWhat sigils can do:|YKO
Early marks improve practical rewards such as corpse ash, profession
materials, salvage returns, and seated recovery. Later marks improve offense,
defense, and elemental affinities, or react to events such as excess healing,
killing blows, repeated hits, and otherwise fatal damage. No sigil grants a
new command.

Type |CKBsigils catalog|YKO for every sigil your character recognizes, its
maximum useful level, where it tends to appear, and a concise description.

Type |YKBsigils|YKO for a table of your active sigils: each combined
level against its maximum, and which piece of equipment supplies it.
The columns are head (H), cloak (C), shoulders (Sh), aura (A), neck
(N1/N2), body (B), legs (L), shield (S), feet (F), rings (R1/R2),
gloves (G), main and secondary weapons (MW/SW), internal equipment (I),
and other sources (O).
A total shown in bright color has reached that sigil's maximum.

